{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.98,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["U10", "U11"],
      "pins": ["U10.4", "U10.5", "U11.4", "U11.5"],
      "nets": ["GND"],
      "observed": "For both isolated CAN transceivers, the logic-side ground (pin 4, GND1) and bus-side ground (pin 5, GND2) are connected to the same GND net.",
      "expected": "To provide the galvanic isolation described in the specification, GND1 and GND2 must remain separate; the bus-side ground should use an isolated return.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"80\") (name \"GND\") ... (node (ref \"U10\") (pin \"4\") (pinfunction \"GND1\")) ... (node (ref \"U10\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"GND2\")) ... (node (ref \"U11\") (pin \"4\") (pinfunction \"GND1\")) ... (node (ref \"U11\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"GND2\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "two isolated CAN buses (CAN0, CAN1)"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The shared ground bypasses the transceivers' galvanic isolation, so the CAN interfaces will not provide the intended isolation from the CM4-side circuitry.",
      "confidence": 0.99
    },
    {
      "category": "wrong_component_type",
      "components": ["U15", "U22", "U35", "U36"],
      "pins": ["U15.4", "U22.4", "U35.4", "U36.4"],
      "nets": ["Net-(U15-Y)", "Net-(U15-A)", "/ESTOP_SINK_ALL", "ESTOP_OUT"],
      "observed": "These e-stop buffers have value SN74LVC1G07QDCKTQ1, but their MPN field specifies U74LVC1G125G-AL5-R. The 1G125 is a push-pull tri-state buffer, not the open-drain buffer specified by the 1G07 value.",
      "expected": "The e-stop sink stages should use the specified SN74LVC1G07 open-drain buffers, or a functionally equivalent open-drain part, so they can sink the loop without actively driving it high.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"U15\") (value \"SN74LVC1G07QDCKTQ1\") ... (field (name \"MPN\") \"U74LVC1G125G-AL5-R\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"17\") (name \"/ESTOP_SINK_ALL\") ... (node (ref \"U35\") (pin \"4\") (pinfunction \"Y\")) ... (node (ref \"U36\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"/OE\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "single non-inverting buffers (SN74LVC1G07, parts U15, U22, U35, U36) wired as /OE-controlled sinks"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If the listed MPN is what gets sourced and assembled, these stages may actively source the e-stop sink/loop instead of acting as open-drain sinks, potentially preventing correct e-stop signaling or causing contention.",
      "confidence": 0.94
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Anomalies are supported by the netlist: both CAN transceivers have their isolation grounds tied together, defeating the specified galvanic isolation. The e-stop buffer MPNs also specify push-pull tri-state parts rather than the open-drain buffer type required by the described sink circuit."
}

